category: Python
requires: alternatives cygwin libgcc1 liblapack0 libopenblas libstdc++6 python312 python312-cffi python312-cython python312-pytest python312-setuptools
sdesc: "Python scientific computing module"
ldesc: "The fundamental package needed for scientific computing with
Python is called NumPy.  This package contains a powerful N-dimensional
array object, sophisticated (broadcasting) functions, tools for
integrating C/C++ and Fortran code, and useful linear algebra, Fourier
transform, and random number capabilities."
external-source: python-numpy

